==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|President||honorifically}}
* {{alt|en|præsident||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|president}}, from {{der|en|la|praesidēns||presiding over; president, leader}} (accusative: {{m|la|praesidentem}}). The Latin word is the substantivized present active participle of the verb {{m|la|praesideō||preside over}}. The verb is composed from {{m|la|prae||before}} and {{m|la|sedeō||sit}}. The original meaning of the verb is 'to sit before' in the sense of presiding at a meeting. A secondary meaning of the verb is 'to command, to govern'. So {{m|la|praesidēns}} means 'the presiding one on a meeting' or 'governor, commander'.

